    "updated_at": "2016-07-14T16:16:17Z",
    "body": "> In our implementation this caused a crash, and even if this were made to work you would get totally unrelated errors when the module was executed (e.g. reference error accessing a binding that should be present).\n\nWhy would you call this an unrelated error? This seems like the correct response to me: you try to import from a module which has previously failed to load, and you get a ReferenceError using that binding.\n",
